"""Fictional, platform-specific troubleshooting cases for each field guide.

The integer sequence selects existing reference rows, so cases never silently
introduce unreferenced commands. Address placeholders must be replaced locally.
"""
CASES={
'fortigate-cli-essentials':('Users report intermittent internet access','A branch firewall appears slow during a busy period. Establish its identity, resource state and forwarding path.',[0,1,2,4], 'A high resource reading during the incident suggests load deserves investigation; a missing expected route points toward forwarding. Either result needs correlation before making a change.', 'Record firmware, affected interfaces and a timed baseline; compare a second sample and verify the route and user experience after the approved fix.'),
'cisco-ios-essentials':('A switch management address stops responding','A previously reachable switch is not answering on its management address.',[0,1,2,3], 'An administratively down interface, an operationally down link and a reachable interface with the wrong address are different findings. Compare the configuration to the expected management network.', 'Retest access from the approved management subnet and confirm that the interface remains up. Capture only the configuration needed for the ticket.'),
'fortigate-routing-arp':('Traffic cannot reach a remote subnet','A client reaches local systems but fails to reach a service on another subnet.',[4,0,1,2], 'A missing or unexpected route directs attention to routing. A directly connected next hop without a resolved ARP entry points to the local link or neighbor.', 'Repeat the route lookup and neighbor check, then test the approved service in both directions.'),
'cisco-interface-diagnostics':('A switch port drops connectivity intermittently','One wired client disconnects while nearby clients remain online.',[0,1,2,3], 'A down link indicates a physical or peer issue; increasing errors while the link is up suggest a link-quality or negotiation issue. Compare two samples.', 'After the approved repair, check link state and error trends again and have the user retest the application.'),
'fortigate-vpn-health':('An IPsec tunnel is up but a service is unreachable','A branch-to-branch application has stopped working even though a VPN appears present.',[0,1,2,4], 'An established tunnel alone is insufficient: compare phase 2 selectors, route, firewall policy and the return path. Counters changing in one direction can guide the next check.', 'Retest the specific application from an approved source and confirm bidirectional traffic counters on the intended tunnel.'),
'cisco-vlans-trunks':('A new VLAN works locally but not across switches','A workstation and gateway are on different switches and the VLAN does not pass the uplink.',[0,1,2,4], 'Check that the access port is in the intended VLAN and the VLAN is allowed and active on the trunk. MAC learning on the expected port helps localize the path.', 'Recheck both ends of the trunk, learned MAC addresses and the gateway test after the approved configuration change.'),
'fortigate-ha-system-health':('The standby firewall shows a health concern','An HA member has an alert following a maintenance window.',[0,2,3,4], 'Compare roles, synchronization and time across members. A mismatch in member state or clock is evidence to investigate; it does not justify an immediate failover.', 'Confirm both members return to the intended cluster state and record the result without forcing a production failover.'),
'cisco-routing-basics':('A router has a route but traffic still fails','A routed service is unreachable from one source network.',[0,4,2,3], 'The most specific route and outgoing interface establish the forward path only. Check next-hop resolution and the destination’s return route separately.', 'Repeat the destination lookup and perform a scoped service test from the affected source after the approved correction.'),
'fortigate-session-inspection':('A policy was changed but a connection behaves unexpectedly','A single client continues to see an old behavior after a firewall policy change.',[0,1,2,4], 'Compare the session’s endpoints, interface and timing with the intended policy and route. Existing sessions can outlive a configuration change.', 'Capture the evidence and follow the approved change procedure before clearing any session; retest a new connection afterwards.'),
'cisco-neighbor-discovery':('The switch uplink connects to an unexpected device','A topology diagram and port label disagree about an uplink.',[0,1,2,4], 'Match local and remote port identifiers, then compare them with the cable record. Missing discovery data can mean the peer has the protocol disabled.', 'Update the inventory only after confirming the physical path; compare the neighbor again after any approved cabling change.'),
'linux-network-essentials':('A Linux server cannot reach its gateway','A server has lost connectivity after a network change.',[0,1,2,4], 'Verify the intended address and route first. A missing or incomplete neighbor entry for a directly connected gateway suggests local link or neighbor resolution trouble.', 'Repeat the address, route and neighbor checks and test the approved destination after the network issue is corrected.'),
'cloud-network-fundamentals':('A private workload cannot reach an internal service','Two workloads in different subnets should communicate over a private address.',[0,1,2,3,4], 'Trace the source subnet, route, network access rules and name resolution in both directions. Provider security controls have different stateful and rule-order semantics.', 'Document the actual path and confirm the service and return traffic after an authorized correction.'),
'windows-network-troubleshooting':('A Windows workstation cannot open an internal site','The browser fails to reach an internal HTTPS application, while the user is connected to the network.',[1,0,2,3,4], 'A failed DNS lookup differs from successful name resolution followed by a failed TCP connection. Compare the selected adapter and DNS server with the expected configuration.', 'Repeat name resolution and the TCP 443 test using the intended service name, then retest in the application.'),
'windows-services-and-event-logs':('An application service stopped during the night','A service is stopped and users report that an application was unavailable in the morning.',[4,1,2,3], 'Align the boot time, service state and system-event timestamps. Cumulative process CPU is not current CPU utilization and a stopped service may be intentional.', 'After the approved service recovery, confirm its state and examine new events; avoid treating a restart alone as the root cause.'),
'active-directory-users-and-groups':('A user cannot access a shared resource','A user can sign in but reports that a newly granted shared-resource permission is not working.',[0,1,2,3,4], 'Confirm the user and domain, account state and relevant direct or nested groups. Group membership is only one input to effective permissions and a fresh sign-in may be relevant.', 'Verify the intended resource access with the user after the approved group or permission change and review propagation where applicable.'),
'active-directory-replication-health':('An account change appears on only one domain controller','An administrator changed an attribute but another site still shows the previous value.',[0,2,3,4,1], 'Identify the affected controller, replication partner and last success. Use the actual error to investigate DNS, connectivity, authentication or topology instead of forcing replication blindly.', 'Confirm subsequent successful replication and compare the affected attribute on the relevant controllers.'),
'microsoft-graph-connection-and-user-lookup':('A Graph query returns an unexpected account result','An administrator is investigating whether a user exists in the intended tenant.',[0,1,2,3], 'The tenant ID and granted scopes determine what the command can read. A permission failure, a wrong tenant and a missing user have different meanings.', 'Run the bounded lookup in the verified tenant, record only necessary fields and disconnect the session.'),
'microsoft-graph-query-and-paging-basics':('A directory export appears incomplete','An administrator compares a small Graph result with an expected full user inventory.',[0,1,2,4], 'A bounded Top result is a sample. Use paging with -All for a full authorized inventory, and compare the selected properties and tenant context.', 'Repeat the bounded comparison and, if required, perform the full inventory under the approved data-handling procedure.'),
'entra-id-sign-in-investigation':('A user is blocked from signing in to one application','A sign-in failure occurs after a policy rollout.',[0,1,2,3,4], 'Compare the failure reason, authentication steps and conditional-access policy result. A report-only policy has no enforcement effect.', 'Retest the same application with the user after an approved policy or identity correction and compare the new sign-in event.'),
'entra-id-devices-and-tenant-overview':('A joined laptop fails an SSO check','A user reports repeated prompts on a Windows device expected to be registered.',[0,1,2,3,4], 'Match device and tenant IDs between the local output and portal. Device join state and the user’s primary refresh token are separate observations.', 'In the affected user session, repeat the local status check and verify the application sign-in after the underlying issue is addressed.'),
'exchange-online-mailbox-inspection':('A mailbox user cannot send messages','A user reports that sending is blocked and an administrator suspects mailbox quota.',[0,1,2,4,3], 'Compare mailbox identity, actual size and configured send quota. A send failure can have other causes, including account or transport restrictions.', 'Verify the mailbox statistics and a user-generated test message after the approved correction; close the admin session.'),
'exchange-online-message-tracing':('A sender says a message never arrived','A recipient reports a missing message sent within the last day.',[0,1,2,4,3], 'Match the sender, recipient, time and trace ID; use the event details for the specific recipient. Transport delivery does not prove the message was read.', 'Record the final trace disposition and verify the recipient’s experience, then disconnect from Exchange Online.'),
'azure-subscription-and-resource-inventory':('A resource is missing from an Azure inventory','An engineer expects to find a resource but the CLI output is empty.',[0,1,2,4,3], 'Confirm the account, tenant and active subscription before interpreting an empty resource list. RBAC can hide resources even in the correct subscription.', 'Repeat the inventory after selecting the authorized subscription and compare resource group and name with the deployment record.'),
'azure-virtual-network-inspection':('A VM cannot reach a private service','A workload in a VNet cannot connect to another private endpoint.',[0,1,2,3,4], 'Compare address spaces, subnet associations, NSGs and route tables. Listed resources are not the same as effective NIC rules or effective routes.', 'Use the provider’s effective-route and connectivity tools for the affected endpoint, then retest the specific service after the approved fix.'),
'sophos-firewall-cli-health-checks':('A firewall seems slow at peak time','An administrator sees intermittent delays and needs a baseline from the Device Console.',[0,1,4,2,3], 'Record firmware, uptime, CPU, memory and disk around the symptom. A single reading cannot prove a memory leak or a restart cause.', 'Collect a second timed sample and correlate with the relevant event logs before proposing changes.'),
'sophos-firewall-traffic-investigation':('A new application flow is blocked','A client cannot reach an application through Sophos Firewall after a rule change.',[0,1,2,4,3], 'A matching drop event and rule ID identify where to investigate. No event may mean logging was not enabled or the filter does not match the original or translated flow.', 'Retest the same source, destination and port after an approved change and compare the corresponding log event.'),
'juniper-junos-cli-essentials':('A Junos device becomes unreachable after maintenance','A monitoring system reports that a Juniper device is offline after planned work.',[0,4,1,2,3], 'Compare software and uptime with the maintenance window, interface admin/link state and chassis alarms. A recent boot does not establish why it happened.', 'Verify the management interface and monitoring from the authorized network and retain relevant alarm details.'),
'juniper-routes-and-neighbor-checks':('A Junos router cannot reach an adjacent network','A remote prefix is unavailable from a Junos device.',[0,4,1,2,3], 'Check the correct routing instance and active next hop, then compare neighbor resolution and physical interface state. LLDP absence alone is not a link test.', 'Repeat the route and neighbor checks and retest the authorized destination after the underlying link or route issue is fixed.'),
'ubiquiti-unifi-device-connectivity':('A UniFi access point appears offline','An access point forwards inconsistently and the UniFi console shows it offline.',[0,1,2,4,3], 'An unexpected or missing management address points toward DHCP or VLAN configuration; an expected address with an offline status calls for management-path checks.', 'After the approved network correction, verify the device is online and reachable without resetting or readopting it unnecessarily.'),
'ubiquiti-unifi-switch-port-checks':('A powered access point does not come online','A UniFi switch port should provide both network access and power to an access point.',[0,1,2,3,4], 'Separate link negotiation, VLAN assignment and available PoE budget. A live link does not by itself prove the management VLAN or power budget is correct.', 'Confirm power and link stability, the intended VLANs and the endpoint status after the approved repair.'),
'hpe-proliant-ilo-health-overview':('A ProLiant server reports degraded health','An operations dashboard reports degraded hardware health on a server.',[0,1,2,3,4], 'Match the serial number first, then correlate health, management events, temperature, fan and power observations. Preserve logs before replacing parts.', 'Confirm the affected component and health state after authorized maintenance and retain relevant events for support.'),
'hpe-aruba-cx-switching-essentials':('An Aruba CX switch port is up but the endpoint is isolated','A device connects physically but cannot reach its expected VLAN.',[0,1,2,3,4], 'Confirm AOS-CX and inspect the port, VLAN membership and neighbor path. A VLAN existing on the switch does not prove it is carried across the uplink.', 'Verify port and VLAN state at both ends and retest the endpoint after the approved change.'),
'dell-poweredge-idrac-health-checks':('A PowerEdge server unexpectedly went offline','A system owner asks whether a hardware event preceded an outage.',[0,1,2,3,4], 'Match the service tag, power status, system events and lifecycle events to the incident time. Reading power status is different from issuing a power action.', 'Preserve the event history and verify system health after approved maintenance; do not reset a running host as a first diagnostic step.'),
'dell-poweredge-hardware-inventory':('A server maintenance plan needs a reliable inventory','An administrator must compare firmware and hardware before a scheduled change.',[0,1,2,4,3], 'Confirm the service tag, versions and inventory, then check hardware events and any queued jobs. An old inventory may not yet reflect a recent component change.', 'Compare the results with the approved baseline and confirm job state before scheduling any update.'),
'dell-data-domain-capacity-and-health':('Backups fail against a Data Domain appliance','A backup job reports errors and the storage team needs the appliance baseline.',[0,1,2,3,4], 'Check DD OS version, filesystem state, physical capacity and current alerts; then inspect relevant replication state. A running filesystem does not guarantee free capacity.', 'Retest a scoped backup after the underlying issue is addressed and confirm capacity and alerts remain healthy.'),
'dell-data-domain-replication-checks':('A replication destination looks behind','A protection team notices that the expected replication destination has not updated.',[0,1,2,3,4], 'Match the context and last synchronization with the expected schedule. An idle context may be normal without new data; compare repeated throughput samples and alerts.', 'Confirm the relevant context completes a new synchronization and document the observed time and status.'),
'kali-nmap-discovery-essentials':('Validate a lab host’s exposed ports','A lab owner asks which of three known TCP services are reachable from an approved test machine.',[0,1,2,4,3], 'Confirm the authorized target and compare host discovery with a bounded connect scan. A filtered port is not proof of which firewall or host caused the filtering.', 'Repeat the same limited scan after the approved change and compare port states and reasons with the original results.'),
'kali-wireshark-packet-analysis':('Investigate a failed connection in a lab capture','A permitted packet capture shows a client unable to connect to a test service.',[2,0,1,3,4], 'Focus on the test endpoint, DNS and the TCP handshake. Retransmissions and missing packets are clues, but capture location and packet loss can affect interpretation.', 'Compare a fresh authorized capture after remediation and protect capture files because they can contain sensitive traffic.'),
'kali-burp-suite-proxy-basics':('Inspect a training application request','A learner needs to understand a harmless request to an authorized local training application.',[0,1,2,4,3], 'Use the built-in browser, inspect the method, path and status in history, and confirm the host belongs to the lab. A paused request must be forwarded to continue browsing.', 'Turn interception off and repeat the same harmless request; close the temporary project according to the lab’s data-handling rules.')}
